# Homebrew casks (macOS only), installed with `brew bundle`.
# Formulae and Mac App Store apps are declared in config/mise/config.toml.
#
# Casks stay with Homebrew instead of mise's `brew-cask:` manager because:
# - mise leaves casks Homebrew installed alone (`apply` and `upgrade` skip
#   them), so moving an existing cask means reinstalling it under mise.
# - Casks mise installs get only mise's receipt, not Homebrew's cask metadata,
#   so `brew upgrade` and `brew uninstall` no longer see them.
# - Reinstalling an app bundle can make macOS drop its privacy permissions
#   (Accessibility for Hammerspoon, Karabiner, CleanShot, PopClip).
# - mise implements only part of the cask artifact types; services, for
#   example, are not supported.
# See https://mise.jdx.dev/bootstrap/packages/brew-cask.html

# Development tools
cask "git-credential-manager"

